														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3714236">
									

<p>I like this a lot. Of all the entries, this was the one that got me most invested in the actual mystery-solving aspect; it hits the right spot between being simple and easy to follow, whilst retaining enough room for thought and nuance and lacking an obvious solution. The characterisation is also well done - it's concise while being detailed enough to invest the reader sufficiently in the characters and remember who is who.</p>
<p>Although I liked the multiple endings as well, and felt they added a lot of rereading mileage to the article, my only gripe would be that their inclusion felt a little forced; I would have accepted them more easily in a piece about an SCP that affected documentation or created parallel dimensions, for example, while there doesn't seem to be any reason for them to be in an article about this object other than wanting to include them for out-of-universe reasons.</p>
<p>PoI-28-Jeannie seems to switch between Kirkwood and Kirkland, which I think is an error unless there's something I'm missing.</p>
<p>Anyway, if this were to win I think it would be a solid choice.</p>

