			<div class="content" id="post-content-3714344">
									

<p>Thank you for the lovely comment! Glad you liked it.</p>
<p>As for the format screw, I did consider giving a stronger implication that there's an in-universe justification for it. The multiple timeline weirdness is an aspect of the anomaly, but not the main focus of it, and thus it got sidelined so as not to detract from the mystery at hand. Perhaps with more time I could have found an elegant way to include that plot thread, but, alas. I do think the format screw fits nicely into the underlying theme of the anomaly, though (i.e. this is what happens when trickster gods play parlor games).</p>
<p>Apparently in my mad dash to finish this, I straight-up forgot what Jeannie's surname was when I went to write the endings. Nice catch.</p>

