			<div class="content" id="post-content-3719263">
									

<p>So, I upvoted this pretty early on; I think it's very strong, and &#8212; while the three ending trick feels a little shoe-horned, the endings themselves are strong enough for them to work for me.</p>
<p>I've got one suggestion &#8212; it's tentative, and not super-important, but since I'm going through these pieces I thought I'd drop it here:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">FEEDBACK</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3306 is a carousel amusement ride located in the Continental Ranges of the Canadian Rockies. It is powered by anomalous means and remains in constant motion.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>When I first read this, the immediate image this opening description gave me was of a carousel sitting on the side of a frozen mountain.</p>
<p>I think this might benefit from putting the carousel somewhere where it's less jarring (but still significantly creepy). A derelict amusement park might be too cliché; an alternative might be an abandoned town or settlement &#8212; or even a warehouse or storage basement (I particularly like this solution, as it's easy to imagine a carousel locked away in a warehouse or underground, and it also prevents the people on the carousel from being affected by inclement weather).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyway, I really enjoyed this one &#8212; good luck with the contest!</p>

